{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ascend — file/upload investigation",
    "description": "Two requests. `1. users (CONTROL)` is known to work and proves the credentials and the HMAC signature are correct. `2. file/upload (UNDER TEST)` uses the identical signing code and returns 500 System error.\n\nRun them in order. If the control returns code 10000 and the upload returns 500, the difference is the endpoint, not the caller.\n\nSet appId, appSecret and userId in the collection variables first. baseUrl defaults to the test environment.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "https://api-mms.newtime.top" },
    { "key": "appId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "appSecret", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "idNumber", "value": "S7790721A" },
    { "key": "phone", "value": "91234567" },
    { "key": "dataJson", "value": "" },
    { "key": "timestamp", "value": "" },
    { "key": "nonce", "value": "" },
    { "key": "sign", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Ascend request signing, identical for both requests below.",
          "//",
          "// HMAC-SHA256 over the parameters: `sign` excluded, empty values",
          "// dropped, keys in ASCII order, joined as key=value with &.",
          "// The digest is UPPERCASE hex - lowercase is rejected with code 600.",
          "// `data` participates as its JSON string.",
          "",
          "const CryptoJS = require('crypto-js');",
          "",
          "const appId  = pm.collectionVariables.get('appId');",
          "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('appSecret');",
          "const data   = pm.collectionVariables.get('dataJson') || '';",
          "",
          "if (!appId || !secret) {",
          "  throw new Error('Set appId and appSecret in the collection variables first.');",
          "}",
          "",
          "const timestamp = String(Date.now());",
          "const nonce = [1e7, 1e3, 4e3, 8e3, 1e11].join('-').replace(/[018]/g, c =>",
          "  (c ^ (crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(1))[0] & (15 >> (c / 4)))).toString(16));",
          "",
          "const params = { appId: appId, timestamp: timestamp, nonce: nonce, data: data };",
          "",
          "const signString = Object.keys(params)",
          "  .filter(k => k !== 'sign')",
          "  .filter(k => params[k] !== undefined && params[k] !== null && params[k] !== '')",
          "  .sort()",
          "  .map(k => k + '=' + params[k])",
          "  .join('&');",
          "",
          "const sign = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(signString, secret)",
          "  .toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex)",
          "  .toUpperCase();",
          "",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('timestamp', timestamp);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('nonce', nonce);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('sign', sign);",
          "",
          "console.log('signed string:', signString);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. users (CONTROL — this one works)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Set the payload BEFORE the collection-level script signs it.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('dataJson', JSON.stringify({",
              "  idNumber: pm.collectionVariables.get('idNumber'),",
              "  phone: pm.collectionVariables.get('phone')",
              "}));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('control returns 10000 — signing and credentials are correct', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('10000');",
              "});",
              "if (body.data && body.data.userId) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.data.userId);",
              "  console.log('userId captured for the upload request:', body.data.userId);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/openApi/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["openApi", "users"] },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"appId\": \"{{appId}}\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"{{timestamp}}\",\n  \"nonce\": \"{{nonce}}\",\n  \"sign\": \"{{sign}}\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"idNumber\": \"{{idNumber}}\",\n    \"phone\": \"{{phone}}\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        "description": "Proves the credentials and the signature are correct. Also captures a real userId into the collection variables for the upload request below."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. file/upload (UNDER TEST — returns 500)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('dataJson', JSON.stringify({",
              "  userId: pm.collectionVariables.get('userId'),",
              "  fileSource: 'web',",
              "  fileBusiness: 'income'",
              "}));",
              "",
              "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('userId')) {",
              "  throw new Error('Run request 1 first — it captures a userId.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('response:', JSON.stringify(body));",
              "pm.test('upload returns 10000', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('10000');",
              "});",
              "if (body.code === '500') {",
              "  console.log('500 System error. The control request above signed identically and succeeded,');",
              "  console.log('so the credentials and signature are not the problem.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/openApi/file/upload", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["openApi", "file", "upload"] },
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            { "key": "file", "type": "file", "src": [], "description": "Attach any PDF, JPG or PNG. The 500 does not depend on the file — a PDF, a real PNG and plain text all behave identically." },
            { "key": "fileInfo", "value": "{{dataJson}}", "type": "text", "description": "The object the documentation names." },
            { "key": "appId", "value": "{{appId}}", "type": "text" },
            { "key": "timestamp", "value": "{{timestamp}}", "type": "text" },
            { "key": "nonce", "value": "{{nonce}}", "type": "text" },
            { "key": "sign", "value": "{{sign}}", "type": "text" }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Signed by the same collection-level script as the control request. Returns {\"code\":\"500\",\"msg\":\"System error\"}.\n\nAlso tried, all with the same result: `data` in place of `fileInfo`; both together; the fileInfo fields flattened as separate form fields; and no signed envelope at all. A malformed request returns 502 Parameter error by Ascend's own error table, so a 500 across every shape points at the endpoint."
      }
    }
  ]
}
